WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.080
Let the rumor slinging commence.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:06.540
A few weeks ago, the guys over at We Got This
Covered reported that, according to undisclosed

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:10.999
sources, Kingsman and Rocketman star Taron
Egerton is high on Marvel's wish list to take

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.740
over the role of Wolverine - and now the star
himself has weighed in on the rumor.

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:19.529
Egerton is currently riding high on the critical
and box office success of the Elton John biopic

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:23.630
Rocketman, in which the actor channeled the
legendary musician to jaw-dropping effect

00:00:23.630 --> 00:00:26.200
- even singing all of the movie's songs himself.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:30.410
And while it seems that Egerton wouldn't necessarily
cast himself as Wolverine if the choice were

00:00:30.410 --> 00:00:34.410
his, he did suggest that he'd be game to take
on the role - or, failing that, any other

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.660
role that Marvel Studios would consider him
for.

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.440
"Are we gonna stand, or are we gonna fight?"

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:45.700
When asked whether there was any substance
to the Wolverine rumor, Egerton said:

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:47.480
"That one I think is just a rumor.

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:49.120
As far as I'm aware, it's unfounded.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:50.760
I don't know if I'm quite grisly enough.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.880
I mean, if the people at Marvel think I am,
then great, let's go.

00:00:53.890 --> 00:00:55.790
But I think there are probably better candidates.

00:00:55.790 --> 00:00:57.780
But I would love to be involved with that
world somewhere."

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.820
"Oh yeah, Charles, we got ourselves an X-Men
fan."

00:01:01.540 --> 00:01:05.680
Despite his reluctance, it's probably fair
to say that Egerton - who has proven his capability

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:09.380
as an action star in the Kingsman series - would
be an excellent choice for the part.

00:01:09.580 --> 00:01:12.860
And that's a sentiment shared by the one guy
who ought to know best.

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:17.110
In 2016, Hugh Jackman - who famously played
Wolverine for a staggering 17 years - was

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:20.890
asked whether he'd be game to appear in a
Deadpool film, while doing the press rounds

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:23.740
for Eddie the Eagle with Egerton - who also
starred in that movie.

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:24.740
Jackman explained:

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.100
"I've never thought about it till now, but
doing something with [Deadpool actor] Ryan

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.720
[Reynolds] - he's awesome - that's always
attractive to me."

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.620
Gesturing to Egerton, Jackman then said:

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.370
"But I think [Marvel has] probably got several
other people lined up to play [Wolverine]…

00:01:36.370 --> 00:01:37.000
probably you."

00:01:37.140 --> 00:01:41.260
It's almost as if Jackman knew something everyone
else didn't, and there's a good chance that

00:01:41.260 --> 00:01:44.020
his comment is what set the rumor mill spinning
in the first place.

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:48.780
At the time, of course, Disney's acquisition
of the film and television assets of Fox Studios

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.560
hadn't yet begun to take shape, but once it
became clear that the X-Men were destined

00:01:52.560 --> 00:01:57.370
to be rebooted into the MCU, Marvel Studios
head honcho Kevin Feige swiftly expressed

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:01.790
his intention to recast the merry band of
mutants with much younger actors, including

00:02:01.790 --> 00:02:02.280
Wolverine.

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:06.320
It makes sense to do just that, of course,
since Marvel famously likes to sign its talent

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:09.940
to long-term contracts, sometimes involving
as many as six pictures.

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:13.840
And while it goes without saying that a number
of X-fans would love to see Jackman reprise

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:18.239
his role in the MCU, it's safe to say that
the 50-year old Jackman probably has no desire

00:02:18.239 --> 00:02:22.310
to go on playing Wolverine - and many of the
fan-favorite choices for the role, such as

00:02:22.310 --> 00:02:27.060
54-year old Keanu Reeves and 41-year old Tom
Hardy - would also face the same problem.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.120
At 29, however, Egerton could hold down the
role for the same length of time that Jackman

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:31.620
did.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:36.340
He's also a remarkably versatile actor, equally
adept at playing a budding superspy as an

00:02:36.349 --> 00:02:41.159
iconic rock star, and - as fans of the famously
stocky superhero will surely appreciate - he's

00:02:41.159 --> 00:02:43.139
only five feet nine inches tall, too.

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:47.130
At any rate, you've got to hope that Egerton
is just being coy about his chances of taking

00:02:47.130 --> 00:02:47.620
the role.

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:52.200
After all, Marvel Studios is practically peerless
when it comes to casting their heroes and

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:55.320
villains, and Egerton as Wolverine could just
be their masterstroke.

